      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The escrow process, a necessary safeguard against the mischievous intentions of a dishonest seller, is a bit like a trusty old watchmaker, carefully guarding the valuable timepieces of your earnest money and down payment funds. In Seattle, the escrow agent acts as a neutral third party, holding onto your funds until the sale is complete and the conditions of the contract are met.\n\nThe legal purpose of escrow is to ensure that the funds are only released to the seller when all the conditions of the sale have been fulfilled, such as the inspection and appraisal reports coming back clean, the title being clear, and the seller has fulfilled their obligations. This setup protects your assets from being stolen or misused by a dishonest seller, as the escrow agent has a fiduciary duty to hold the funds until the sale is complete.\n\nThink of it like a secure, high-walled fortress, where the escrow agent is the gatekeeper, carefully monitoring the funds and only allowing them to be released when the conditions are met. This way, you can rest assured that your earnest money and down payment funds are safe and secure, even if the seller tries to pull a fast one on you.",
      "source": "target",
